      "difficulty": "X",
      "skill_tags": ["algebraic_fractions", "forming_equations", "word_problem"],
      "problem_text": "A tank can be filled by pipe A in $x$ hours and by pipe B in $(x+3)$ hours. Together they take 2 hours. Find $x$.",
      "answer": "$x = 3$ hours",
      "solution": "Rates: A fills $\\frac{1}{x}$ per hour, B fills $\\frac{1}{x+3}$ per hour. Combined: $\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x+3}=\\frac{1}{2}$. Multiply by $2x(x+3)$: $2(x+3)+2x=x(x+3)$, $4x+6=x^2+3x$, $x^2-x-6=0$, $(x-3)(x+2)=0$, $x=3$ or $x=-2$ (reject). So $x=3$ hours."
